      }
    ],
    "missing": [
      {
        "what": "Per-topic MCQ threshold: Qwen 0.5B scores 0% on cloud deployment at design level while every 3B+ model scores 100%. This is a sharp jump rather than a smooth trend.",
        "locator": "Section V.A; Fig. 7",
        "versions": "V6"
      },
      {
        "what": "FR judge scores vs parameters per cognitive level (analyze, design, implement), which the authors say scale consistently with size.",
        "locator": "Fig. 6; Fig. 3",
        "versions": "V6"
      }
    ],
    "verdict_notes": "The size comparisons are confounded: within-family 'sizes' mix generations (Llama 3.2, 3, 3.3; Qwen 2.5 vs Qwen3-Coder, which is code-specialised). Free-response scores come from a single LLM judge, and no uncertainty is reported. The evidence for V6 is therefore weak and qualitative, not a test of predictability. The paper cites Kaplan et al. but does not engage with scaling laws directly."
  },
